<title>FRANCE: Iraq wheat purchase reaches 300,000 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Iraq wheat purchase reaches 300,000 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq bought a total of 300,000 tonnes of wheat under the United Nations oil-for-food agreement on Thursday, European grain traders said.</p>
<p>Two thirds of the wheat will come from France and the remaining 100,000 tonnes from Australia, they said. Iraq is now negotiating to buy another 100,000 tonnes of optional-origin wheat which would come from a producing nation of the seller's choice, they said.</p>
</text>
